{"version":"1","id":"regehr","handle":"regehr","name":"Embedded in Academia","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/184fb345011042d887308ece6c5e5f92","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-1.9615,"y":-3.8785,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":10,"newest_post_at":"2024-09-04T18:29:03.000Z","oldest_post_at":"2020-06-17T16:17:48.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.0,"listicle_ratio":0.0,"question_ratio":0.0,"avg_read_time":5.3,"summary_length_avg":281.8,"title_length_avg":67.8,"title_length_var":308.56,"tag_entropy":1.390438,"tag_diversity":0.5,"top_tag_share":0.1,"avg_upvotes":0.0,"median_upvotes":0.0,"avg_comments":0.0,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":1.0,"zero_engagement_share":1.0,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":0.291355,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.111111},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-9.4559,-8.5588],"cadence_depth":[-9.8824,-1.5588],"hype_variety":[-4.8971,-9.8529],"title_style":[-4.9412,-5.6765]},"top_tags":[["general-programming",5],["computer-science",5],["compiler",2],["compiler-optimization",1],["career",1]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["Dataflow Analyses and Compiler Optimizations that Use Them, for Free \u2013 Embedded in Academia","Looking for Missed Alarm Bugs in a Formal Verification Tool \u2013 Embedded in Academia","Responsible and Effective Bugfinding \u2013 Embedded in Academia"],"outlier":["llvm-reduce \u2013 Embedded in Academia"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"bCi0e0h2I","title":"Looking for Missed Alarm Bugs in a Formal Verification Tool \u2013 Embedded in Academia","url":"https://blog.regehr.org/archives/2124","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/looking-for-missed-alarm-bugs-in-a-formal-verification-tool-embedded-in-academia-bci0e0h2i","summary":"Formal verification tools like Alive2, used for translation validation in LLVM IR, face challenging defects such as false alarms and missed alarms. Detecting missed alarm bugs involves sophisticated methods including using a random program generator like YARPGen and the LLVM superoptimizer Minotaur. These tools rigorously test to ensure Alive2's reliability, essential for maintaining compiler optimization accuracy. Despite extensive testing, completely ruling out missed alarms remains uncertain.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/e7f66331bcf7f038013d2e2b7b95cde9?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-09-04T18:29:03.000Z"},{"id":"NzY0QZvQP","title":"Dataflow Analyses and Compiler Optimizations that Use Them, for Free \u2013 Embedded in Academia","url":"https://blog.regehr.org/archives/2578","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/dataflow-analyses-and-compiler-optimizations-that-use-them-for-free-embedded-in-academia-nzy0qzvqp","summary":"This post discusses the importance of dataflow analyses in compiler optimizations and proposes methods to automate the creation and use of such analyses. It also suggests implementing missing dataflow analyses, such as congruences, in LLVM.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--foaA6JGU--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2004","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-04-20T21:55:33.000Z"},{"id":"vPxhjFIEG","title":"Formal-Methods-Based Bugfinding for LLVM\u2019s AArch64 Backend \u2013 Embedded in Academia","url":"https://blog.regehr.org/archives/2265","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/formal-methods-based-bugfinding-for-llvm-s-aarch64-backend-embedded-in-academia-vpxhjfieg","summary":"This post discusses the use of formal methods to find and report defects in LLVM compiler's middle end optimizers and extending the work to cover one of LLVM's backends. It explores the refinement relation, the process of lifting compiled AArch64 code into Alive2 IR, and the bugs that have been found in the AArch64 backend.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--VDukGCjf--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2002","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-06-06T14:58:02.000Z"},{"id":"lRWa1U0Vj","title":"High-Throughput, Formal-Methods-Assisted Fuzzing for LLVM \u2013 Embedded in Academia","url":"https://blog.regehr.org/archives/2148","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/high-throughput-formal-methods-assisted-fuzzing-for-llvm-embedded-in-academia-lrwa1u0vj","summary":"This post discusses the use of mutation-based fuzzing for LLVM optimization passes. It introduces a custom mutator for LLVM IR and describes the results of fuzzing with this mutator. Bugs found using alive-mutate are also highlighted.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/af8c16dcd2d17d33122c17d13a7aadcf?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-05-31T14:56:41.000Z"},{"id":"Hq38cWwC4","title":"llvm-reduce \u2013 Embedded in Academia","url":"https://blog.regehr.org/archives/2109","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/llvm-reduce-embedded-in-academia-hq38cwwc4","summary":"llvm-reduce is a tool for reducing LLVM IR through automated test-case reduction. It is specific to LLVM IR and has advantages in terms of efficiency and effectiveness. It is part of LLVM and can be obtained by building or downloading LLVM.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--foaA6JGU--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2004","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2021-05-13T16:58:00.000Z"},{"id":"XR3qkkGPU","title":"Responsible and Effective Bugfinding \u2013 Embedded in Academia","url":"https://blog.regehr.org/archives/2037","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/responsible-and-effective-bugfinding-embedded-in-academia-xr3qkkgpu","summary":"Learn about responsible and effective bug finding, the importance of collaboration between bug finders and software developers, and the factors contributing to the rise of external bug finding.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--HRgLpUt6--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2003","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2020-08-17T18:36:43.000Z"},{"id":"JWLrcdaso","title":"Alive2 Part 3: Things You Can and Can\u2019t Do with Undef in LLVM \u2013 Embedded in Academia","url":"https://blog.regehr.org/archives/1837","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/alive2-part-3-things-you-can-and-can-t-do-with-undef-in-llvm-embedded-in-academia-jwlrcdaso","summary":"The functions 'add' and 'shift' in LLVM have different behaviors and can't be safely substituted. Undef in LLVM can be replaced with various values, but the replacement should be a subset of the original value set. Undefined behavior in an IR is not necessarily related to source-level undefined behavior.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/93e43858ca8cbf23dd81261494449149?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2020-07-31T20:33:05.000Z"},{"id":"YcIzJ4Omy","title":"The Gods Pocket Peak Trail \u2013 Embedded in Academia","url":"https://blog.regehr.org/archives/1832","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-gods-pocket-peak-trail-embedded-in-academia-ycizj4omy","summary":"Explore the remote Jarbidge Wilderness and hike the challenging Gods Pocket Peak Trail, which offers stunning views and unique microclimates.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/b4f1723edec79c23df4917fc531ff0ce?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2020-07-23T15:41:01.000Z"},{"id":"epHEPQiKk","title":"You Might as Well Be a Great Copy Editor \u2013 Embedded in Academia","url":"https://blog.regehr.org/archives/1471","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/you-might-as-well-be-a-great-copy-editor-embedded-in-academia-ephepqikk","summary":"The importance of copy editing in the writing process and recommended resources for improving copy editing skills.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--OHB84bZF--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2010","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2020-06-24T15:28:14.000Z"},{"id":"mQ8yHgwfQ","title":"The Saturation Effect in Fuzzing \u2013 Embedded in Academia","url":"https://blog.regehr.org/archives/1796","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-saturation-effect-in-fuzzing-embedded-in-academia-mq8yhgwfq","summary":"Fuzzing can experience saturation where the number of new bugs found by a fuzzer drops off over time, either due to the bugs being triggered at low probability or because some bugs are out of reach for the fuzzer. Saturation can be detected using coverage-based stopping criteria or by splitting a testing effort into subsets with their own coverage measure. Mitigating saturation can be done by finding more bugs before saturation occurs through wider net casting and adding new mutation operators for mutation-based fuzzers.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--2-1xRawN--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2011","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2020-06-17T16:17:48.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["ns","80lv","koaning","alligator","richg42"],"opposite_handles":["dailydevworld","horde","on_leuwcq","watercooler","dotnetsquad"],"similar":[{"id":"ns","handle":"ns","name":"NativeScript","is_squad":false,"x":-2.1775,"y":-3.7629,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":63,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/ns","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.682239,"median_upvotes":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.039683,"avg_read_time":0.0,"tag_diversity":0.52381},"top_tags_preview":[["nativescript",56],["general-programming",17],["ios",11]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-9.0735,-4.1471],"cadence_depth":[-3.0294,-10.0],"hype_variety":[7.6618,-5.5147],"title_style":[5.4118,-9.6912]}},{"id":"80lv","handle":"80lv","name":"80 LEVEL","is_squad":false,"x":-2.1882,"y":-4.0758,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":1915,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/78eebcd76c154e6bbfd565fed7dc4093","features_preview":{"posts_pe